# Lockeroom Database — Architecture & Business Rules

This workspace integrates with the Lockeroom Supabase database. **Full reference:** `docs/lockeroom-architecture.md` (mirrored from [lockeroom_schema](https://github.com/Lockeroom-Gym/lockeroom_schema)). Below is a fast-load summary of the most critical rules.

---

## Database

- **Provider:** Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- **Project ID:** `dvrhazdtbsttzduaedzu`
- **Source of truth:** `docs/lockeroom-architecture.md`

---

## Core Tables (quick ref)

| Table | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `member_database` | Member demographics and primary coach assignment |
| `member_memberships` | One row per membership term — central operational table |
| `member_newsale_metadata` | Financial snapshot for new sales |
| `member_renewal_meta` | Financial snapshot for renewals |
| `member_not_renewing` | Churn tracking — who's leaving and why |
| `member_holds` | Membership pauses |
| `member_daily_sessions_attended` | Actual session attendance |
| `member_lcns` | Late cancels and no-shows |
| `staff_database` | All staff, coaches, and roles |
| `work_estimations` | Per-client hour allocations per role |
| `system_config` | Session durations and contract hour baselines |
| `membership_types` | Membership product definitions |
| `membership_versions` | Historical pricing and policy snapshots |
| `member_physicals_raw` | Physical assessment data — movement screen, benchmarks, focus/avoid fields. One row per assessment. |
| `member_health_metrics` | InBody body composition scans — weight, bf, smm, inbody_score, date_created. |

